  'tow-capacity': {"title":"Tow Capacity Calculator: GCWR, Truck Weight & Passengers","metaDesc":"Free Tow Capacity Calculator: get the safe towing weight instantly, with every step of the math shown. Nothing leaves your browser.","canonicalPath":"/auto/tow-capacity","cat":"auto","catName":"Auto & Transport","lsi":["tow capacity calculator trailer weight payload","tow capacity formula","how to calculate tow capacity","safe towing weight formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does the Tow Capacity Calculator do?</h2>\n<p>Tow Capacity Calculator works out the safe towing weight from the GCWR, Truck Weight, and Passengers + Cargo, following standard Auto & Transport conventions — the page defaults produce a safe towing weight of 2400 kg max trailer.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> GCWR, Truck Weight, and Passengers + Cargo.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the safe towing weight, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> the standard Auto & Transport formula, evaluated entirely in your browser.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (gcwr of 5,000, truck weight of 2,200, passengers + cargo of 400), tow capacity calculator returns a safe towing weight of 2400 kg max trailer. Assumptions and limits are summarized below.</p><h2>How does the Tow Capacity Calculator work?</h2>\n<p>Tow Capacity Calculator computes the safe towing weight directly from your inputs — the GCWR, Truck Weight, and Passengers + Cargo feed the formula. Nothing is uploaded: the math runs locally in your browser and the result appears as you type.</p>","desc":"<h2>How the Tow Capacity Calculator works</h2>\n<p>Tow Capacity Calculator answers one question well — given the values you provide, what is the safe towing weight? Enter the GCWR, Truck Weight, and Passengers + Cargo, and the result panel returns the value with the full working underneath.</p>\n<h2>Using the Tow Capacity Calculator</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>GCWR</strong> — one of the values tow capacity calculator builds the calculation from; the result reflects exactly what you type here.</li>\n<li><strong>Truck Weight</strong> — used in the first stage of the calculation in tow capacity calculator, so entering it accurately matters more than any later refinement.</li>\n<li><strong>Passengers + Cargo</strong> — the value tow capacity calculator feeds directly into its formula — match it to the scenario you are modeling before moving on.</li>\n<li>Note the safe towing weight. It updates as you type, and the worked steps below it in tow capacity calculator make the arithmetic auditable.</li>\n<li>Adjust and re-run. Change one input at a time to see how sensitive the safe towing weight is to it — the fastest way to understand what tow capacity calculator is doing.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>The relationship between the inputs is fixed by the formula, and Tow Capacity Calculator makes each substitution explicit so nothing about the safe towing weight is hidden.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with gcwr of 5,000, truck weight of 2,200, passengers + cargo of 400, tow capacity calculator returns <strong>2400 kg max trailer</strong>. The same run reports GCWR: 5000 kg.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Loaded truck = 2200 + 400 = 2600 kg</li><li>Max trailer = GCWR − loaded truck = 5000 − 2600 = 2400 kg</li></ul><p>Substitute your own values and the same steps produce your answer — that is the point of a calculator that shows its working.</p>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>The safe towing weight is the headline answer; the supporting figures beneath it and the step list in Tow Capacity Calculator give the surrounding context needed to judge it.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>Tow Capacity Calculator fits planning and checking: tow capacity planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the safe towing weight, or any moment when the safe towing weight needs to be right the first time.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>Entering a rate or percentage in the wrong scale (5 versus 0.05, or the reverse) is a frequent trap — the labels in Tow Capacity Calculator show the expected scale, and the steps reveal a misapplied value.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Bookmark tow capacity calculator — after the first visit it works offline, so the safe towing weight is one tap away even without a connection.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>Very large or very small inputs can push the safe towing weight from Tow Capacity Calculator beyond what is practically meaningful — sanity-check extreme values before relying on them.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Because it is fast and private — Tow Capacity Calculator runs entirely in your browser, nothing is uploaded, and no account is needed.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does the Tow Capacity Calculator calculate?","a":"Tow Capacity Calculator is built for tow capacity questions that need a defensible number: the working is always visible, the inputs accept your own values, and the safe towing weight updates as you type. Because the safe towing weight arrives with supporting figures and a full step list, Tow Capacity Calculator gives you context rather than a single bare number."},{"q":"How is the safe towing weight calculated?","a":"The first steps are loaded truck = 2200 + 400 = 2600 kg, then max trailer = gcwr − loaded truck = 5000 − 2600 = 2400 kg. Precision is maintained through every intermediate step inside Tow Capacity Calculator, and rounding is applied only when the final value is formatted."},{"q":"What do I need to use the Tow Capacity Calculator?","a":"The GCWR, Truck Weight, and Passengers + Cargo that tow capacity calculator asks for, or the page defaults if you just want to see the calculation work. Each input maps directly to the formula, and changing any one of them recalculates the safe towing weight instantly."},{"q":"What does the result from the Tow Capacity Calculator mean?","a":"The main number tow capacity calculator returns is the safe towing weight for your exact inputs, and the supporting figures and step list give it context. Inputs outside a reasonable range may produce a safe towing weight that is mathematically correct but practically implausible; the steps panel in Tow Capacity Calculator helps you spot that quickly."},{"q":"When is the Tow Capacity Calculator most useful?","a":"Typical uses for Tow Capacity Calculator include tow capacity planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the safe towing weight — anywhere the figure needs to be defensible rather than guessed. The result is shareable — the link carries your inputs, so a colleague can open the same calculation in Tow Capacity Calculator without retyping it."}]},
