  'crypto-gains': {"title":"Crypto Gains Calculator: Buy Price, Sell Price & Quantity","metaDesc":"Free Crypto Gains Calculator: enter the Buy Price and Sell Price and get a profit of $7462.50. Every step shown, nothing leaves your browser.","canonicalPath":"/finance/crypto-gains","cat":"finance","catName":"Finance","lsi":["crypto gains calculator cryptocurrency profit loss","crypto gains formula","how to calculate crypto gains","profit formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does the Crypto Gains Calculator do?</h2>\n<p>Crypto Gains Calculator works out the profit from the Buy Price, Sell Price, and Quantity, following standard Finance conventions — the page defaults produce a profit of $7462.50.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Buy Price, Sell Price, and Quantity.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the profit, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> the standard Finance formula, evaluated entirely in your browser.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (buy price of 30,000, sell price of 45,000, quantity of 0.5), crypto gains calculator returns a profit of $7462.50. Assumptions and limits are summarized below.</p><h2>How does the Crypto Gains Calculator work?</h2>\n<p>Crypto Gains Calculator computes the profit directly from your inputs — the Buy Price, Sell Price, and Quantity feed the formula. Nothing is uploaded: the math runs locally in your browser and the result appears as you type.</p>","desc":"<h2>How the Crypto Gains Calculator works</h2>\n<p>At its core, Crypto Gains Calculator takes the Buy Price, Sell Price, and Quantity and evaluates the standard formula step by step, so the profit can be checked rather than trusted on faith.</p>\n<h2>Using the Crypto Gains Calculator</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Buy Price</strong> — a core input crypto gains calculator applies in the formula — keep the units consistent with the label.</li>\n<li><strong>Sell Price</strong> — one of the values crypto gains calculator builds the calculation from; the result reflects exactly what you type here.</li>\n<li><strong>Quantity</strong> — used in the first stage of the calculation in crypto gains calculator, so entering it accurately matters more than any later refinement.</li>\n<li>Review the output. Beyond the headline profit, crypto gains calculator lists the intermediate steps — useful for catching a mistyped input.</li>\n<li>Iterate. Vary the inputs one at a time; the movement in the profit shows which lever matters most for your crypto gains question.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>Crypto Gains Calculator lists every intermediate step in the result panel, so the derivation of the profit can be checked line by line.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with buy price of 30,000, sell price of 45,000, quantity of 0.5, crypto gains calculator returns <strong>Profit: $7462.50</strong>. The same run reports Return: 49.75% | Fees: $37.50.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Cost basis = $30000 × 0.5 = $15000.00</li><li>Proceeds = $45000 × 0.5 = $22500.00</li><li>Fees = ($15000.00 + $22500.00) × 0.1% = $37.50</li><li>Gain = $22500.00 − $15000.00 − $37.50 = $7462.50</li></ul><p>Substitute your own values and the same steps produce your answer — that is the point of a calculator that shows its working.</p>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>Interpret the profit against the inputs that produced it — the same number from different inputs can mean different things, which is why Crypto Gains Calculator always shows the pairing.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>Typical uses for Crypto Gains Calculator include crypto gains planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the profit — anywhere the figure needs to be defensible rather than guessed.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>Rounding intermediate values by hand introduces error Crypto Gains Calculator does not have; it keeps full precision internally, so trust the displayed profit over mental arithmetic.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> If the profit looks wrong, read the steps panel before re-entering anything; it usually shows exactly where the number in Crypto Gains Calculator departed from expectation.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>Results from Crypto Gains Calculator are estimates computed from the values entered; real-world outcomes can differ when fees, taxes, or conditions not modeled here apply.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Because comparing scenarios takes seconds: change one input at a time in Crypto Gains Calculator and watch the profit move, which is the fastest way to understand what drives it.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does the Crypto Gains Calculator calculate?","a":"Crypto Gains Calculator keeps the whole calculation in front of you — the Buy Price, Sell Price, and Quantity, the formula, the intermediate steps, and a worked example you can reproduce line by line. Because the page doubles as documentation: Crypto Gains Calculator puts the formula, a worked example, and the assumptions right beside the calculator."},{"q":"How is the profit calculated?","a":"The first steps are cost basis = $30000 × 0.5 = $15000.00, then proceeds = $45000 × 0.5 = $22500.00. The calculation in Crypto Gains Calculator applies the standard Finance method, keeping full precision internally and rounding only the final display."},{"q":"What do I need to use the Crypto Gains Calculator?","a":"The Buy Price, Sell Price, and Quantity that crypto gains calculator asks for, or the page defaults if you just want to see the calculation work. Each input maps directly to the formula, and changing any one of them recalculates the profit instantly."},{"q":"What does the result from the Crypto Gains Calculator mean?","a":"The main number crypto gains calculator returns is the profit for your exact inputs, and the supporting figures and step list give it context. Treat the profit from Crypto Gains Calculator as a planning figure rather than a binding quote, and confirm important decisions with the relevant professional."},{"q":"When is the Crypto Gains Calculator most useful?","a":"Common scenarios for Crypto Gains Calculator: crypto gains planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the profit. The step list makes it equally useful for learning the method and for double-checking someone else's numbers. Run Crypto Gains Calculator twice with deliberately low and high inputs; the spread tells you how sensitive the profit is, which a single run never shows."}]},
