  'body-fat-fitness': {"title":"Body Fat % from BMI: Weight, Height & Age","metaDesc":"Free Body Fat % from BMI: enter the Weight and Height and get a body fat percentage of 19.8%. Every step shown, nothing leaves your browser.","canonicalPath":"/fitness/body-fat-fitness","cat":"fitness","catName":"Fitness & Exercise","lsi":["body fat percentage from bmi","body fat estimate without calipers","deurenberg body fat formula","body fat bmi formula","how to calculate body fat","body fat percentage formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does the Body Fat % from BMI do?</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI works out the body fat percentage from the Weight, Height, and Age, following standard Fitness & Exercise conventions — the page defaults produce a body fat percentage of 19.8%.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Weight, Height, and Age.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the body fat percentage, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> the standard Fitness & Exercise formula, evaluated entirely in your browser.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (weight of 70, height of 170, age of 30), body fat % from bmi returns a body fat percentage of 19.8%. Assumptions and limits are summarized below.</p><h2>How does the Body Fat % from BMI work?</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI computes the body fat percentage directly from your inputs — the Weight, Height, and Age feed the formula. Nothing is uploaded: the math runs locally in your browser and the result appears as you type.</p>","desc":"<h2>How the Body Fat % from BMI works</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI is built for body fat bmi questions that need a defensible number: the working is always visible, the inputs accept your own values, and the body fat percentage updates as you type.</p>\n<h2>Using the Body Fat % from BMI</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Weight</strong> — the value body fat % from bmi feeds directly into its formula — match it to the scenario you are modeling before moving on.</li>\n<li><strong>Height</strong> — a core input body fat % from bmi applies in the formula — keep the units consistent with the label.</li>\n<li><strong>Age</strong> — one of the values body fat % from bmi builds the calculation from; the result reflects exactly what you type here.</li>\n<li>Check the result. The body fat percentage is shown as soon as the inputs are valid, and the steps beneath it show exactly how body fat % from bmi derived it.</li>\n<li>Explore. Each input change in body fat % from bmi recalculates instantly; watching the body fat percentage move tells you which factor dominates your case.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>Precision is maintained through every intermediate step inside Body Fat % from BMI, and rounding is applied only when the final value is formatted.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with weight of 70, height of 170, age of 30, body fat % from bmi returns <strong>19.8%</strong>. The same run reports BMI: 24.2 | Deurenberg formula | Category: Average.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Formula (Deurenberg et al., 1991):</li><li>BF% = 1.20 × BMI + 0.23 × age − 10.8 × sex − 5.4 (sex: male=1, female=0)</li><li>BMI = weight / height² = 70 / 1.70² = 24.2</li><li>BF% = 1.20×24.2 + 0.23×30 − 10.8 − 5.4 = 19.8%</li></ul><p>Substitute your own values and the same steps produce your answer — that is the point of a calculator that shows its working.</p>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>The result panel in Body Fat % from BMI leads with the body fat percentage and follows with intermediate values; if the headline surprises you, the steps usually reveal which input is responsible.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>Common scenarios for Body Fat % from BMI: body fat bmi planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the body fat percentage. The step list makes it equally useful for learning the method and for double-checking someone else's numbers.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>Entering a rate or percentage in the wrong scale (5 versus 0.05, or the reverse) is a frequent trap — the labels in Body Fat % from BMI show the expected scale, and the steps reveal a misapplied value.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> The result is shareable — the link carries your inputs, so a colleague can open the same calculation in Body Fat % from BMI without retyping it.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI assumes the units shown in each label — entering values in different units will skew the body fat percentage proportionally.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Because the body fat percentage arrives with supporting figures and a full step list, Body Fat % from BMI gives you context rather than a single bare number.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does the Body Fat % from BMI calculate?","a":"This page is a working body fat % from bmi: enter your values, read the body fat percentage, and follow the step list to see exactly how the answer was derived. Because Body Fat % from BMI works the same on phone and desktop, keeps working offline after the first visit, and never asks for sign-up."},{"q":"How is the body fat percentage calculated?","a":"The first steps are formula (deurenberg et al., 1991):, then bf% = 1.20 × bmi + 0.23 × age − 10.8 × sex − 5.4 (sex: male=1, female=0). Rounding in Body Fat % from BMI follows standard display conventions — the underlying math keeps several decimal places until the body fat percentage is shown."},{"q":"What do I need to use the Body Fat % from BMI?","a":"The Weight, Height, and Age that body fat % from bmi asks for, or the page defaults if you just want to see the calculation work. Each input maps directly to the formula, and changing any one of them recalculates the body fat percentage instantly."},{"q":"What does the result from the Body Fat % from BMI mean?","a":"The main number body fat % from bmi returns is the body fat percentage for your exact inputs, and the supporting figures and step list give it context. The model behind Body Fat % from BMI covers the standard case; special cases, edge values, or jurisdiction-specific rules may need manual adjustment."},{"q":"When is the Body Fat % from BMI most useful?","a":"Students, planners, and professionals use body fat % from bmi for body fat bmi planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the body fat percentage, and for sanity-checking numbers that arrived from somewhere else. Bookmark body fat % from bmi — after the first visit it works offline, so the body fat percentage is one tap away even without a connection."}]},
