  'vo2-max': {"title":"VO2 Max Calculator: 1.5 Mile Run & Age","metaDesc":"Free VO2 Max Calculator: enter the 1.5 Mile Run and Age and get a vo2 max of 71.3 ml/kg/min. Every step shown, nothing leaves your browser.","canonicalPath":"/health/vo2-max","cat":"health","catName":"Health","lsi":["vo2 max calculator","vo2 max formula","how to calculate vo2 max","vo2 max formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does the VO2 Max Calculator do?</h2>\n<p>VO2 Max Calculator works out the vo2 max from the 1.5 Mile Run and Age, following standard Health conventions — the page defaults produce a vo2 max of 71.3 ml/kg/min.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> 1.5 Mile Run and Age.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the vo2 max, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> the standard Health formula, evaluated entirely in your browser.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (1.5 mile run of 12, age of 25), vo2 max calculator returns a vo2 max of 71.3 ml/kg/min. Assumptions and limits are summarized below.</p><h2>How does the VO2 Max Calculator work?</h2>\n<p>VO2 Max Calculator computes the vo2 max directly from your inputs — the 1.5 Mile Run and Age feed the formula. Nothing is uploaded: the math runs locally in your browser and the result appears as you type.</p>","desc":"<h2>How the VO2 Max Calculator works</h2>\n<p>Use VO2 Max Calculator when the vo2 max needs to be right the first time: it evaluates your inputs against the standard Health method and shows the working, not just the answer.</p>\n<h2>Using the VO2 Max Calculator</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>1.5 Mile Run</strong> — a core input vo2 max calculator applies in the formula — keep the units consistent with the label.</li>\n<li><strong>Age</strong> — one of the values vo2 max calculator builds the calculation from; the result reflects exactly what you type here.</li>\n<li>Review the output. Beyond the headline vo2 max, vo2 max calculator lists the intermediate steps — useful for catching a mistyped input.</li>\n<li>Iterate. Vary the inputs one at a time; the movement in the vo2 max shows which lever matters most for your vo2 max question.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>The engine behind VO2 Max Calculator evaluates the inputs in a single pass — no hidden iterations or adjustments — so the vo2 max you see is exactly what the formula produces for the values you entered.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with 1.5 mile run of 12, age of 25, vo2 max calculator returns <strong>VO2 Max: 71.3 ml/kg/min</strong>. The same run reports Good fitness.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Formula (Cooper 1.5-mile run):</li><li>Male: VO2 = 110 - 2.6×time - 0.3×age</li><li>Female: VO2 = 100 - 2.4×time - 0.3×age</li><li>VO2 = 71.3 ml/kg/min</li></ul><p>Substitute your own values and the same steps produce your answer — that is the point of a calculator that shows its working.</p>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>Interpret the vo2 max against the inputs that produced it — the same number from different inputs can mean different things, which is why VO2 Max Calculator always shows the pairing.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>Typical uses for VO2 Max Calculator include vo2 max planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the vo2 max — anywhere the figure needs to be defensible rather than guessed.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>Copying the vo2 max without its assumptions is the frequent error — the number from VO2 Max Calculator is valid for exactly the inputs shown, so carry the context with it.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> If the vo2 max looks wrong, read the steps panel before re-entering anything; it usually shows exactly where the number in VO2 Max Calculator departed from expectation.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>Treat the vo2 max from VO2 Max Calculator as a planning figure rather than a binding quote, and confirm important decisions with the relevant professional.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Because comparing scenarios takes seconds: change one input at a time in VO2 Max Calculator and watch the vo2 max move, which is the fastest way to understand what drives it.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does the VO2 Max Calculator calculate?","a":"Every run of VO2 Max Calculator evaluates the 1.5 Mile Run and Age you enter, applies the standard Health formula, and reports the vo2 max with each step listed for review. Because the page doubles as documentation: VO2 Max Calculator puts the formula, a worked example, and the assumptions right beside the calculator."},{"q":"How is the vo2 max calculated?","a":"The first steps are formula (cooper 1.5-mile run):, then male: vo2 = 110 - 2.6×time - 0.3×age. The formula operates on the values exactly as entered; keeping the units shown in each label is what makes the vo2 max from VO2 Max Calculator trustworthy."},{"q":"What do I need to use the VO2 Max Calculator?","a":"The 1.5 Mile Run and Age that vo2 max calculator asks for, or the page defaults if you just want to see the calculation work. Each input maps directly to the formula, and changing any one of them recalculates the vo2 max instantly."},{"q":"What does the result from the VO2 Max Calculator mean?","a":"The main number vo2 max calculator returns is the vo2 max for your exact inputs, and the supporting figures and step list give it context. Very large or very small inputs can push the vo2 max from VO2 Max Calculator beyond what is practically meaningful — sanity-check extreme values before relying on them."},{"q":"When is the VO2 Max Calculator most useful?","a":"Common scenarios for VO2 Max Calculator: vo2 max planning, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the vo2 max. The step list makes it equally useful for learning the method and for double-checking someone else's numbers. Run VO2 Max Calculator twice with deliberately low and high inputs; the spread tells you how sensitive the vo2 max is, which a single run never shows."}]},
